+## 2026-09-12 19:57 UTC — Onboarding-flow branch merge strategy
+**Decision:** `obase` and `sloww/onboarding-flow` independently built the
+same 5-step onboarding flow (Faculty -> Department -> Year -> Course ->
+Quick Test/Mastery/Upload) under two different route trees, neither
+aware of the other. Resolution: keep `obase`'s route tree
+(`/faculties/...`) and its course-detail/Quick Test implementation
+(the only one of the two with a working, executable test session —
+`sloww`'s equivalent screen was a "Coming soon" placeholder). Retire
+`sloww`'s parallel `/onboarding/...` pages. Keep everything else
+`sloww` built that `obase` never touched: the persistent Tools nav
+shell, Transcript tracker, Path-to-first-class SVG, CGPA
+calculator/converter, Upload Course Material screen — rewire these to
+point at `obase`'s surviving onboarding routes instead of the retired
+`/onboarding/...` ones.
+**Context:** Neither branch's commits or DECISIONS.md entries reference
+the other; this was two agents solving the same doctrine steps in
+parallel, not a deliberate fork. `obase` added no new migration and
+reuses main's schema as-is; `sloww` added migrations
+`0003_seed_onboarding_content` and `0004_enrollments`, whose `0003`
+filename collides with main's already-merged
+`cgpa_0003_taxonomy_and_keystone` — not a verbatim collision (different
+content, same sequence number), so left as-is per founder call, same
+class of non-blocking collision main's own `3c36f48` commit fixed for a
+different pair. Anonymous (unauthenticated) course submission via
+`obase`'s `submit-course` endpoint is accepted as correct for now —
+founder's stated reason: only the dev team currently holds links to the
+demo, so there's no real anonymous-public exposure yet; auth gating
+returns as a doctrine item once the app is public.
+**Status as of this entry:** merge not yet executed in code — this
+entry records the resolved strategy for whichever agent performs the
+merge, not confirmation that it has happened.
